-- title:
--   Level raising at q ∣ N: parabolicity, adjointness, Hecke commutation
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a local integral domain of characteristic zero, let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$ which is not a unit in $\mathcal O$, let $N$ and $q$ be nonzero naturals with $q$ prime and $q \mid N$, and let `h1`, `hq'` be instances of [`CohCarrier.LevelLE`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L330) for the pair of levels $N \mid Nq$ with trivial character groups and degrees $1$ and $q$ (so $N \mid Nq$, $d \mid Nq/N$, and the reduction condition, vacuous for $\top$). Write $H^1(M) = \mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_0(M), \mathcal O)$ for [`CohCarrier.H1 M ⊤ 𝒪`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L162) (additive homomorphisms from [`CohCarrier.GammaH M ⊤`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the copy of $\Gamma_0(M)$ in $SL_2(\mathbb Z)$, to $\mathcal O$), let [`ModularCurve.Period.parabolicHoms`](def/ModularCurve_PeriodMap.html#L62) be the submodule of those homomorphisms vanishing on parabolic elements, let $U_q =$ [`CohCarrier.heckeTL N ⊤ 𝒪 q`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L23) (pull-back along conjugation by the upper matrix attached to $q$, followed by transfer), and let $\iota_d^* =$ [`CohCarrier.iDegL`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L401) (pull-back along conjugation by the lower matrix attached to $d$) and $j_d =$ [`CohCarrier.jDegL`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L492) (transfer along the image of that map). Put $W = \iota_q^* \circ U_q - q\,\iota_1^{*}\colon H^1(N) \to H^1(Nq)$ and $V = U_q \circ j_1 - q\,j_q\colon H^1(Nq) \to H^1(N)$. The conclusion is the conjunction of five assertions: $W$ maps parabolic homomorphisms at level $N$ to parabolic homomorphisms at level $Nq$; $V$ maps parabolic homomorphisms at level $Nq$ to parabolic homomorphisms at level $N$; for parabolic $x, jy$ at level $N$ and $y, wx$ at level $Nq$ with $wx = W x$ and $jy = V y$, the pairings satisfy [`CuspForm.Bfam₀ 𝒪 N jy x = CuspForm.Bfam₀ 𝒪 (N*q) y wx`](def/CuspForm_CornerPairingFamily.html#L140), i.e. $W$ and $V$ are adjoint for the pairings [`CuspForm.Bfam₀`](def/CuspForm_CornerPairingFamily.html#L140); for every nonzero prime $\ell \neq q$, $W$ commutes with the Hecke operators [`CohCarrier.heckeT`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L250) at $\ell$ on all of $H^1(N)$ (no parabolicity assumed); and, for every set $S$ of naturals, every element $b$ of the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O} H^1(N)$ generated by the range of [`CohCarrier.opFamily N ⊤ S 𝒪`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) (the operators `heckeTL` at the primes of the generating family together with the diamond operators `diamondL`) preserves parabolic homomorphisms at level $N$ and is self-adjoint for [`CuspForm.Bfam₀ 𝒪 N`](def/CuspForm_CornerPairingFamily.html#L140), in the sense that $B(bx, y) = B(x, by')$ whenever $bx = b x$ and $by' = b y$ with all four elements parabolic.
--
--   These are the properties of the level-raising degeneracy maps between the cohomology of $X_0(N)$ and $X_0(Nq)$ at a prime $q$ dividing the level, in the combination $\iota_q^* U_q - q\,\iota_1^*$ and its adjoint $U_q j_1 - q\,j_q$, as used in Wiles's level-raising argument at primes dividing the level. The statement supplies the parabolicity, adjointness and Hecke-equivariance needed to transport a Hecke module realised as a local corner of $H^1(\Gamma_0(N),\mathcal O)$ through one such step, and is cited in the construction of a corner realisation at the raised level.
-- source:
